From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Gmeiner <cgmeiner@igalia.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Mar 2026 15:52:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 19/57] panfrost: Add FS clip distance prolog NIR builder

Build a standalone fragment shader prolog that loads gl_ClipDistance
values from CLIP_DIST0/CLIP_DIST1 with perspective-correct
interpolation, multiplies by gl_FragCoord.w to recover linear
interpolation, and demotes fragments where any clip distance is
negative. Demote keeps helper invocations alive so derivatives in the
main FS stay defined.

This is compiled independently against the VS's varying layout and
runs in front of the main FS. The new skip_atest compile input avoids
a second ATEST alongside the main FS's, which would overwrite the
coverage mask.

Modeled after src/asahi/lib/agx_nir_prolog_epilog.c.

Signed-off-by: Christian Gmeiner <cgmeiner@igalia.com>
Reviewed-by: Olivia Lee <olivia.lee@collabora.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/40343>
